# ThreadSanitizer suppressions of the Linux guest run (ws213-p004, the design's
# 9 節 "Linux の TSan"). Only the Vulkan driver and LLVM inside it are
# suppressed here; a report between the compositor's existing threads goes
# below with its reason and a Bug ticket (asked of Q1); nothing of WS213's own
# threads (input, cursor, render) or locks is ever suppressed.
# race: and deadlock: lines name the module (matched against each frame), not
# called_from_lib:, which aborts the run when the loader unloads the driver
# (T1-549: "library ... matched against called_from_lib suppression ... is
# unloaded").
race:libvulkan_lvp.so
race:libvulkan_virtio.so
race:libvulkan_intel.so
race:libvulkan_radeon.so
race:libLLVM
deadlock:libvulkan_lvp.so
deadlock:libvulkan_virtio.so
deadlock:libvulkan_intel.so
deadlock:libvulkan_radeon.so
deadlock:libLLVM
